[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Perspective explores two named tables under a registered Aurora theme

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-PERSPECTIVE-VIEW
TITLE: Perspective explores two named tables under a registered Aurora theme
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
perspective.js loads the pinned CDN modules, builds two named tables (nodes,
relations) on one client worker, and drives one viewer. The Nodes|Relations
switch loads the target Table object and then restores that table's saved or
default configuration: restore({table}) alone merges the OLD view's columns
into the NEW table's schema and is refused, so the switch rides the deprecated
load(table) path instead (measured; WORK-BOARD-TABLE-SWITCH-UNDEPRECATE owns
the exit). Config-update events save the native token per table to
localStorage. Aurora is a REGISTERED Perspective theme: assets/theme.css
carries a quoted --psp-theme-name on a bare perspective-viewer selector for
auto-discovery, overrides the --psp-* variables under the theme-scoped
selectors, themes the popup custom elements separately (they are not viewer
descendants), and rides the CDN pro-dark.css base -- linked with crossorigin,
without which a cross-origin stylesheet's rules are unreadable and the theme
silently never appears -- for icons, labels and defaults.
<<<
